{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"agent_message","text":"The direct real-source call now passes. The callback leg showed a second PHP-specific gap: source closures are represented as identity-bearing `Closure` values around their internal function cells, so TS can store and return one but PHP wasn’t exposing a common entry on that value for foreign invocation. I’m adding that structural entry projection to the existing closure constructor, delegating to its already-created cell so calls preserve the original closure value."}}
